# SCHEMA RULES

## Architecture

One Organization = one dedicated database.

Do not add organization_id to every table.

Hierarchy:
School → Academic Year → Branch → Class → Section → Student.

## Integrity

Every schema change must review:
- PK;
- FK;
- UNIQUE;
- CHECK;
- NOT NULL;
- default;
- delete behavior;
- historical preservation.

## History

Never overwrite historical academic placement when promotion, transfer or section change occurs.

## Delete

Never delete protected historical data.

Never use CASCADE DELETE casually.

A record with no dependent/protected data may be deleted only if the approved lifecycle explicitly permits it.

## Subjects

Subject is Organization-level master.
SchoolSubject controls school availability.
ClassSubject controls class assignment.

Never duplicate a subject because another school/class uses it.

## Identity

User ID and domain IDs such as Student ID and Teacher ID are distinct concepts.

Do not use labels as PKs.

## Academic year

Do not merge records merely because the displayed year/class name is identical.
